### Summary

I'm using Nginx as a reverse proxy for my Streamlit app running on `localhost:8502`. I want to rewrite URLs such that requests to `http://localhost/assist` are transformed into `http://localhost/?p=assist`.  

However, after applying the rewrite, WebSocket connections for Streamlit fail. These WebSocket requests are attempting to communicate with URLs like `/assist/_stcore/...`, which causes the WebSocket to break.  

#### **Current Nginx Configuration:**  

```nginx
upstream streamlit {
    server 127.0.0.1:8502;
}

server {
    listen 80;

    # Only rewrite URLs that do NOT contain "_stcore"
    if ($request_uri !~ "_stcore") {
        rewrite ^/([^/?]+)$ /?p=$1 break;
    }

    location /_stcore/stream {
        proxy_pass http://streamlit/_stcore/stream;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_read_timeout 86400;
    }

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://streamlit;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    }
}
```

#### **Expected Behavior:**  
- Requests like `GET /assist` should become `GET /?p=assist`, and Streamlit should load the page as expected without issues.  
- WebSocket connections used by Streamlit should function correctly, allowing interactions with the app.  

#### **Observed Behavior:**  
- The WebSocket attempts to reach `/assist/_stcore/...` leading to connection errors.  
- The page never fully loads due to these broken WebSocket connections.  


Any help on how to fix this issue while maintaining both the URL rewrite and WebSocket functionality would be greatly appreciated! 🙏

